From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: report charge threshold set failures

Both charge control threshold setters return 0 whatever the firmware
request returned. When the request fails or times out, which happens on
firmware without charge control, userspace sees the write succeed and a
threshold that never applies. Return the request's error.
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -715,7 +715,7 @@
 		battmgr->info.charge_ctrl_end = target_soc;
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qcom_battmgr_set_charge_end_threshold(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr, int end_soc)
@@ -736,7 +736,7 @@
 		battmgr->info.charge_ctrl_end = end_soc;
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qcom_battmgr_charge_control_thresholds_init(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr)
